    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt"><i>Quorum</i>.
    While the Nasdaq Rules require that the quorum for purposes of any meeting of the holders of a listed Company&#8217;s common voting
    stock, as specified in the Company&#8217;s bylaws, be no less than 33 1/3% of the Company&#8217;s outstanding issued and outstanding
    share capital, under Cayman Islands law, a company is entitled to determine in its articles of association the number of shareholders
    and percentage of holdings required for a quorum at a shareholders meeting. Our amended and restated articles of association provides
    that a quorum for a general meeting consists of any one or more persons holding or representing by proxy not less than one-third
    of our outstanding shares carrying the right to vote at such general meeting.</span></td></tr>
