<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify; margin: 0pt"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">The
Company uses the Monte Carlo Model to value the Series B Warrants. Under the Monte Carlo Simulation Model, the share price result paths
and corresponding exercise prices and the number of shares issuable upon the exercise were derived. Each Series B Warrant Share resulted
from Monte Carlo Simulation Model is the input for the Black-Scholes Model, and then the fair value of the warrants was derived by the
trial values as of the valuation date based on the mean of the total trial values. Since Series B Warrants have no expiration, the Company
adopts the <span id="xdx_904_eus-gaap--SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1_dtY_c20241001__20250930__us-gaap--ValuationTechniqueAxis__custom--MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholesMember__us-gaap--ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis__custom--SeriesAWarrantsMember__us-gaap--AwardTypeAxis__custom--TenYearMember_zRGlGBplTuY8" title="Expected life (years)"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2024-10-012025-09-30_custom_MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholesMember_custom_SeriesAWarrantsMember_custom_TenYearMember" format="ixt-sec:duryear" id="Fact002011" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1">10</ix:nonNumeric></span>-year and <span id="xdx_90D_eus-gaap--SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1_dtY_c20241001__20250930__us-gaap--ValuationTechniqueAxis__custom--MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholesMember__us-gaap--ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis__custom--SeriesAWarrantsMember__us-gaap--AwardTypeAxis__custom--FifteenYearMember_zIv214Rgv5ma" title="Expected life (years)"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2024-10-012025-09-30_custom_MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholesMember_custom_SeriesAWarrantsMember_custom_FifteenYearMember" format="ixt-sec:duryear" id="Fact002013" name="us-gaap:SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1">15</ix:nonNumeric></span>-year terms as inputs into the Black-Scholes Model, and the final result is taken as the average of the <span id="xdx_90F_eus-gaap--SharebasedCompensationArrangementBySharebasedPaymentAwardFairValueAssumptionsExpectedTerm1_dtY_c20250908__20250908__us-gaap--ValuationTechniqueAxis__custom--MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholesMember__us-gaap--ClassOfWarrantOrRightAxis__custom--SeriesAWarrantsMember__us-gaap--AwardTypeAxis__custom--TenYearMember_zUQr8xGcxJbj" title="Expected life (years)"><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="From2025-09-082025-09-08_custom_MonteCarloModelAndBlackScholes